IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ncat-claims`

-- Civil and Administrative Tribunal Act 2013 (NSW) -- worked cases for every exported question in ncat-claims.l4.
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text; none was copied from the encoding's output. Each
-- assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Dates are illustrative.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases`

`d` MEANS `the calendar date`
`any day` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 1 2026

§§ `ss 28-31 -- jurisdiction`

-- Arguments: legislation gives an appeal to the Tribunal; ADR Act review; legislation lets the Tribunal decide.
#ASSERT `Which kind of jurisdiction is my matter in` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `external appeal jurisdiction (s 31)`
#ASSERT `Which kind of jurisdiction is my matter in` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `administrative review jurisdiction (s 30)`
#ASSERT `Which kind of jurisdiction is my matter in` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST `general jurisdiction (s 29)`
#ASSERT `Which kind of jurisdiction is my matter in` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Which kind of jurisdiction is my matter in` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST `external appeal jurisdiction (s 31)`
#ASSERT `Which kind of jurisdiction is my matter in` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST `administrative review jurisdiction (s 30)`

§§ `Part 3A -- federal matters`

`may grant` MEANS `the court may grant leave for my application or appeal to be made to it instead of the Tribunal`
`cannot grant` MEANS `the court cannot grant leave on these facts`
`not until` MEANS `the court cannot grant leave until the appeal already lodged is determined`

-- Arguments: standing; first made to the Tribunal; federal jurisdiction; Tribunal otherwise has jurisdiction; within the
-- court's limit; an earlier appeal pending.
#ASSERT `Can I take my matter to a court instead` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `may grant`
#ASSERT `Can I take my matter to a court instead` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `not until`
#ASSERT `Can I take my matter to a court instead` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `cannot grant`
#ASSERT `Can I take my matter to a court instead` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `cannot grant`
#ASSERT `Can I take my matter to a court instead` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `cannot grant`
#ASSERT `Can I take my matter to a court instead` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `cannot grant`
#ASSERT `Can I take my matter to a court instead` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `cannot grant`
#ASSERT `Can I take my matter to a court instead` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `cannot grant`

`saved` MEANS `taken to have started in the court on the day I first made it to the Tribunal, despite any limitation period`
`not saved` MEANS `taken to have started on the day I first made it to the Tribunal, but section 34C(2) does not save it from the limitation period`

-- Arguments: leave granted; day first lodged with the Tribunal; last day of the limitation period.
#ASSERT `How my court proceedings are taken to have started` TRUE (d 10 3 2026) (d 10 3 2026) EQUALS `saved`
#ASSERT `How my court proceedings are taken to have started` TRUE (d 11 3 2026) (d 10 3 2026) EQUALS `not saved`
#ASSERT `How my court proceedings are taken to have started` TRUE (d 9 3 2026) (d 10 3 2026) EQUALS `saved`
#ASSERT `How my court proceedings are taken to have started` TRUE (d 1 1 2027) (d 31 12 2026) EQUALS `not saved`
#ASSERT `How my court proceedings are taken to have started` FALSE (d 9 3 2026) (d 10 3 2026) EQUALS `section 34C applies only once the court grants leave`

