§§ `s 43 and the court appeals -- does a challenge stop the decision`

`no order` MEANS `no order has been made`
`stay` MEANS `an order staying the decision, or otherwise stopping it operating`
`let operate` MEANS `an order letting the decision operate while the appeal is pending`

#ASSERT `Does my challenge stop the decision` `a general application to review a decision of someone outside the Tribunal` `no order` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does my challenge stop the decision` `a general application to review a decision of someone outside the Tribunal` `stay` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does my challenge stop the decision` `an external appeal to the Tribunal` `stay` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does my challenge stop the decision` `an external appeal to the Tribunal` `no order` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does my challenge stop the decision` `an internal appeal to the Appeal Panel` `no order` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does my challenge stop the decision` `an internal appeal to the Appeal Panel` `let operate` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does my challenge stop the decision` `an administrative review application` `stay` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Does my challenge stop the decision` `an administrative review application` `no order` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Does my challenge stop the decision` `an appeal to a court under Part 6 Division 3` `no order` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does my challenge stop the decision` `an appeal to a court under Part 6 Division 3` `stay` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does my challenge stop the decision` `an appeal to a court under Schedule 3 clause 17 or 18 or Schedule 5 clause 29` `no order` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does my challenge stop the decision` `an appeal to the Supreme Court from the Guardianship Division under Schedule 6 clause 14` `no order` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does my challenge stop the decision` `an appeal to the Supreme Court from the Guardianship Division under Schedule 6 clause 14` `stay` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does my challenge stop the decision` `an appeal to the Supreme Court from the Guardianship Division under Schedule 6 clause 14` `let operate` EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 45 -- representation`

`AEOD` MEANS `the Administrative and Equal Opportunity Division`
`CCD` MEANS `the Consumer and Commercial Division`
`OccD` MEANS `the Occupational Division`
`GD` MEANS `the Guardianship Division`
`lawyer` MEANS `an Australian legal practitioner`
`other person` MEANS `another person who is not a practising lawyer`
`entitled` MEANS `I am entitled to be represented by that person without the Tribunal's leave`
`with leave` MEANS `I may be represented by that person, because the Tribunal has granted leave`
`only with leave` MEANS `I may be represented by that person only if the Tribunal grants leave; otherwise I conduct my own case`

-- Arguments: Division; representative; Fair Trading Act legal assistance; Retail Leases Act; s 175 care Act; leave.
#ASSERT `Can I be represented` `AEOD` `lawyer` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `entitled`
#ASSERT `Can I be represented` `AEOD` `other person` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `only with leave`
#ASSERT `Can I be represented` `AEOD` `other person` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `with leave`
#ASSERT `Can I be represented` `CCD` `lawyer` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `only with leave`
#ASSERT `Can I be represented` `CCD` `lawyer` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `entitled`
#ASSERT `Can I be represented` `CCD` `other person` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `only with leave`
#ASSERT `Can I be represented` `CCD` `other person` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `entitled`
#ASSERT `Can I be represented` `CCD` `lawyer` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `entitled`
#ASSERT `Can I be represented` `CCD` `lawyer` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `with leave`
#ASSERT `Can I be represented` `OccD` `lawyer` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `entitled`
#ASSERT `Can I be represented` `OccD` `other person` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `only with leave`
#ASSERT `Can I be represented` `GD` `lawyer` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `entitled`
#ASSERT `Can I be represented` `GD` `lawyer` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `only with leave`
#ASSERT `Can I be represented` `GD` `other person` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `only with leave`
#ASSERT `Can I be represented` `GD` `lawyer` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `only with leave`
#ASSERT `Can I be represented` `AEOD` `other person` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `only with leave`

§§ `s 50 -- hearings`

`leave step` MEANS `deciding whether to grant leave for an external or internal appeal`
`resolution` MEANS `a resolution process, such as conciliation or mediation`
`the matter` MEANS `deciding the matter itself`
`required` MEANS `a hearing is required`
`not required` MEANS `no hearing is required`
`irregular` MEANS `no hearing is required, but the order dispensing with it was made without first hearing from the parties, which is an irregularity the Tribunal may set aside`

-- Arguments: step; Guardianship substantive; procedural rules dispense; order dispensing; opportunity for submissions.
#ASSERT `Must there be a hearing` `leave step` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not required`
#ASSERT `Must there be a hearing` `leave step` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not required`
#ASSERT `Must there be a hearing` `the matter` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `required`
#ASSERT `Must there be a hearing` `resolution` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `required`
#ASSERT `Must there be a hearing` `resolution` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not required`
#ASSERT `Must there be a hearing` `the matter` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not required`
#ASSERT `Must there be a hearing` `the matter` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `not required`
#ASSERT `Must there be a hearing` `the matter` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `irregular`
#ASSERT `Must there be a hearing` `the matter` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `required`
#ASSERT `Must there be a hearing` `the matter` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `required`

§§ `s 55 and Schedule 4 clause 10 -- dismissal`

`withdrew` MEANS `I withdrew my application or appeal`
`frivolous` MEANS `the Tribunal considers my proceedings frivolous, vexatious, misconceived or lacking in substance`
`no show` MEANS `I failed to appear`
`want of prosecution` MEANS `the Tribunal considers there has been a want of prosecution`

-- Arguments: what happened; every applicant did the same; C&C applicant unreasonably disadvantaging another.
#ASSERT `Can my application be dismissed` `withdrew` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can my application be dismissed` `withdrew` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can my application be dismissed` `no show` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can my application be dismissed` `no show` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can my application be dismissed` `frivolous` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can my application be dismissed` `want of prosecution` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can my application be dismissed` `none of these` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can my application be dismissed` `none of these` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- Arguments: dismissed for failure to appear; reasonable explanation.
#ASSERT `Can my dismissed proceedings be reinstated` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can my dismissed proceedings be reinstated` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can my dismissed proceedings be reinstated` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can my dismissed proceedings be reinstated` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Arguments: Consumer and Commercial Division; Tribunal's opinion; who.
#ASSERT `What can be done about a party causing disadvantage` TRUE TRUE `the applicant` EQUALS `the Tribunal may dismiss or strike out the proceedings, or part of them`
#ASSERT `What can be done about a party causing disadvantage` TRUE TRUE `a party other than the applicant` EQUALS `the Tribunal may decide the proceedings, or part of them, in the applicant's favour, or strike the other party out`
#ASSERT `What can be done about a party causing disadvantage` TRUE FALSE `the applicant` EQUALS `clause 10 does not apply`
#ASSERT `What can be done about a party causing disadvantage` FALSE TRUE `a party other than the applicant` EQUALS `clause 10 does not apply`

