§§ `s 60 -- costs`

`may not award` MEANS `each party pays its own costs, and the Tribunal may not award costs`
`own costs` MEANS `each party pays its own costs: costs can be awarded only for special circumstances, and the Tribunal is not satisfied there are any`
`special` MEANS `costs may be awarded because the Tribunal is satisfied there are special circumstances; it decides who pays and how much`

-- Arguments: proceedings; special circumstances.
#ASSERT `Who pays the costs` `a Working with Children decision (Child Protection (Working with Children) Act 2012)` TRUE EQUALS `may not award`
#ASSERT `Who pays the costs` `an NDIS worker check decision (National Disability Insurance Scheme (Worker Checks) Act 2018)` FALSE EQUALS `may not award`
#ASSERT `Who pays the costs` `an administrative review of a victims support decision (Victims Rights and Support Act 2013)` TRUE EQUALS `may not award`
#ASSERT `Who pays the costs` `an administrative review of a victims support decision (Victims Rights and Support Act 2013)` FALSE EQUALS `may not award`
#ASSERT `Who pays the costs` `proceedings under the Dormant Funds Act 1942` FALSE EQUALS `costs are in the Tribunal's discretion`
#ASSERT `Who pays the costs` `proceedings under the Dormant Funds Act 1942` TRUE EQUALS `costs are in the Tribunal's discretion`
#ASSERT `Who pays the costs` `any other proceedings` TRUE EQUALS `special`
#ASSERT `Who pays the costs` `any other proceedings` FALSE EQUALS `own costs`

