§§ `s 62 and Schedule 6 clause 11 -- reasons`

`may request` MEANS `I may request a written statement of reasons within 28 days of being given notice of the decision`
`already` MEANS `a written statement of reasons has already been provided to me`
`no right` MEANS `section 62(2) gives no right to request reasons for this kind of decision`

-- Arguments: kind; a party argued special circumstances for costs; reasons already provided.
#ASSERT `Can I ask for reasons` `any other decision` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `may request`
#ASSERT `Can I ask for reasons` `any other decision` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `already`
#ASSERT `Can I ask for reasons` `a decision dispensing with a hearing under section 50(2)` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no right`
#ASSERT `Can I ask for reasons` `a decision to grant an adjournment` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no right`
#ASSERT `Can I ask for reasons` `a decision not to award costs` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no right`
#ASSERT `Can I ask for reasons` `a decision not to award costs` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `may request`
#ASSERT `Can I ask for reasons` `a decision not to award costs` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `already`
#ASSERT `Can I ask for reasons` `a decision to award costs in the Consumer and Commercial Division, or in an internal appeal from it` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no right`
#ASSERT `Can I ask for reasons` `an order made with the consent of the parties` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no right`
#ASSERT `Can I ask for reasons` `a minor procedural decision with no final or determinative effect on my rights` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no right`

#ASSERT `Will I get guardianship reasons without asking` `any other Guardianship Division decision` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Will I get guardianship reasons without asking` `a decision about consent to minor treatment (Guardianship Act 1987 s 36)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Will I get guardianship reasons without asking` `a decision under Part 5A of the Guardianship Act 1987 (reciprocal arrangements)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Will I get guardianship reasons without asking` `an ancillary or interlocutory decision` EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- 28 days counted from the day after notice: 1 May + 28 = 29 May; 10 February 2028 + 28 = 9 March 2028 (a leap
-- February); 15 December 2026 + 28 = 12 January 2027.
