§§ `ss 32, 80 -- internal appeals`

`first instance` MEANS `the Tribunal at first instance, in a general or administrative review matter`
`final` MEANS `any other decision, ancillary or final`
`interlocutory` MEANS `an interlocutory decision`
`law` MEANS `a question of law`
`other grounds` MEANS `other grounds (fact, or fact and law)`
`ordinary` MEANS `none of the special kinds`
`as of right` MEANS `I may appeal to the Appeal Panel as of right`
`leave only` MEANS `I may appeal to the Appeal Panel only with its leave`
`law only` MEANS `I may appeal to the Appeal Panel on a question of law only, as of right, and not on other grounds even with leave`
`no internal appeal` MEANS `no internal appeal lies against this decision`

-- Arguments: party; who decided; kind of decision; ground; special kind.
#ASSERT `Can I appeal to the Appeal Panel` TRUE `first instance` `final` `law` `ordinary` EQUALS `as of right`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal to the Appeal Panel` TRUE `first instance` `final` `other grounds` `ordinary` EQUALS `leave only`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal to the Appeal Panel` TRUE `first instance` `interlocutory` `law` `ordinary` EQUALS `leave only`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal to the Appeal Panel` TRUE `first instance` `a decision as to costs` `other grounds` `ordinary` EQUALS `leave only`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal to the Appeal Panel` TRUE `first instance` `a decision made with the consent of the parties` `law` `ordinary` EQUALS `as of right`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal to the Appeal Panel` FALSE `first instance` `final` `law` `ordinary` EQUALS `only a party to the proceedings in which the decision was made may appeal`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal to the Appeal Panel` TRUE `the Tribunal imposing a civil penalty in its general jurisdiction` `final` `law` `ordinary` EQUALS `no internal appeal`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal to the Appeal Panel` TRUE `a registrar, in a kind of decision declared internally appealable` `final` `law` `ordinary` EQUALS `as of right`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal to the Appeal Panel` TRUE `a registrar, in any other kind of decision` `final` `law` `ordinary` EQUALS `no internal appeal`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal to the Appeal Panel` TRUE `an Appeal Panel` `final` `law` `ordinary` EQUALS `no internal appeal`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal to the Appeal Panel` TRUE `the Tribunal in an external appeal` `final` `law` `ordinary` EQUALS `no internal appeal`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal to the Appeal Panel` TRUE `the Tribunal in contempt or civil penalty enforcement proceedings under this Act` `final` `law` `ordinary` EQUALS `no internal appeal`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal to the Appeal Panel` TRUE `first instance` `final` `law` `a Working with Children or NDIS worker check decision` EQUALS `no internal appeal`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal to the Appeal Panel` TRUE `first instance` `final` `law` `a decision under the lands legislation` EQUALS `no internal appeal`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal to the Appeal Panel` TRUE `first instance` `final` `law` `a Native Title (New South Wales) Act 1994 Part 7 determination` EQUALS `no internal appeal`
