§§ `ss 82-84 and the Division Schedules -- appeals to courts`

`AP from Tribunal` MEANS `a decision of an Appeal Panel in an internal appeal from the Tribunal`
`SC leave law` MEANS `to the Supreme Court, with its leave, on a question of law only`
`SC law` MEANS `to the Supreme Court, as of right, on a question of law`
`SC law or leave` MEANS `to the Supreme Court, as of right on a question of law, or with its leave on other grounds`
`SC leave` MEANS `to the Supreme Court, only with its leave`
`law ground only` MEANS `not on that ground: the appeal lies on a question of law only`
`guardianship decision` MEANS `an internally appealable decision of the Tribunal in the Guardianship Division`

-- Arguments: party; decision; kind; ground; senior judicial officer; Guardianship internal appeal standing.
#ASSERT `Can I appeal to a court` TRUE `AP from Tribunal` `final` `law` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `SC leave law`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal to a court` TRUE `AP from Tribunal` `final` `other grounds` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `law ground only`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal to a court` FALSE `AP from Tribunal` `final` `law` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `only a party to the proceedings may appeal`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal to a court` TRUE `a decision of the Tribunal in an external appeal` `interlocutory` `law` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `SC leave law`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal to a court` TRUE `a decision of an Appeal Panel in an internal appeal from a registrar` `final` `law` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no appeal to a court lies under this Act against this decision`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal to a court` TRUE `a decision in proceedings in which a civil penalty was imposed on me` `final` `law` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `SC law`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal to a court` TRUE `a decision in proceedings in which a civil penalty was imposed on me` `final` `law` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `to the District Court, as of right, on a question of law`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal to a court` TRUE `a decision in proceedings in which a civil penalty was imposed on me` `final` `other grounds` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `law ground only`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal to a court` TRUE `a decision in proceedings for contempt of the Tribunal` `final` `law` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not under Part 6: a contempt decision is appealed under District Court Act 1973 s 201, as applied by section 73`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal to a court` TRUE `a Working with Children or NDIS worker check decision of the Administrative and Equal Opportunity Division` `final` `law` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `SC law`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal to a court` TRUE `a Working with Children or NDIS worker check decision of the Administrative and Equal Opportunity Division` `final` `other grounds` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `law ground only`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal to a court` TRUE `a lands legislation decision of the Administrative and Equal Opportunity Division` `final` `other grounds` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `to the Land and Environment Court`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal to a court` TRUE `a profession decision of the Occupational Division under the Legal Profession Uniform Law (NSW)` `final` `law` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `to the Supreme Court, by way of rehearing`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal to a court` TRUE `a profession decision of the Occupational Division under the Legal Profession Uniform Law (NSW)` `a decision as to costs` `law` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `SC leave`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal to a court` TRUE `any other profession decision of the Occupational Division` `final` `other grounds` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `SC law or leave`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal to a court` TRUE `any other profession decision of the Occupational Division` `a decision made with the consent of the parties` `law` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `SC leave`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal to a court` TRUE `any other profession decision of the Occupational Division` `interlocutory` `law` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `SC leave`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal to a court` TRUE `guardianship decision` `final` `law` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `SC law or leave`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal to a court` TRUE `guardianship decision` `interlocutory` `law` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `SC leave`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal to a court` TRUE `guardianship decision` `a decision as to costs` `other grounds` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `SC law or leave`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal to a court` TRUE `guardianship decision` `final` `law` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not while my internal appeal stands, unless it is withdrawn with the Appeal Panel's approval`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal to a court` TRUE `any other decision of the Tribunal at first instance` `final` `law` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not to a court under this Act: the decision goes first to an internal appeal`

